Z||000017||Jeff Wendt||12-30-2001||08:42 PM||||Is my thinking wrong here?  My daughter turns 16 in  1.5 years and I am seriously thinking about putting her into a Fiero for the following reasons:<P>1.  They say teenage drivers are easily   distracted by friends in the car.  A 2 seater will reduce the possibility of distractions.<P>2.  Holds up in crashes.  Pictures above look nasty but glad to hear okay.  Govt  and other tests confirmed this.  My wife walked away from 5 car pile up in our 84SE.  Rear ended by pickup doing 55 into stopped traffic.  Car totaled.<P>3.  If I make it a stick, very few friends will be able to or want to drive it.<P>She is not touching my stock 88 GT.  My wife says our family needs two more Fieros!  Oh ya!||||reg||5
Z||000018||Axmanmkii||12-30-2001||08:50 PM||||I've gotten my GS when I was 17. Worked up the whole $4k, while helping my mom pay her bills, by myself. It was a beater. It still looks like one, but it runs like new. All I need to do is remove some dents, and get it painted and it'll be mint. <P>But I cant go without a car for the time it'll take to have those perform, which is why I'm looking at a Fiero. Then I can switch between the two cars when I cant drive one or the other.<P>LOL, my dad is pissed off jealous cause he didnt get a car untill he was 27. Heh, sucks to be him I guess.||||reg||1
